  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nBroad surface ridge is expected to remain east of the Rockies for \nthe next week. A developing trough is expected off the eastern \nseaboard leading to the development of a rex block. This rex block, \nthat evolves into an omega block across the lower 48 will lead to a \nstagnant weather pattern.  Locally, this will lead to dry conditions \nwith temperatures building back into the 70s and 80s (>70 percent \nchance of above normal temperatures Wednesday and beyond).   With \nthe Gulf closed and dry air mass in place, temperatures are expected \nto fall into the upper 30s-lower 40s tonight, potentially leading to \npatchy frost in a few low lying locations. 925 hpa temperatures warm \na few degrees each day leading to the warming trend. \n\nPattern is expected to begin to break down late next week as east \ncoast trough weakens and shifts southwest along the coast. A \ndeepening trough along the west coast will gradually inch \neastward late in the week, leading to building rain chances next\nweekend, though the trend has been towards a slower solution \nkeeping precipitation chances just beyond the seven day \nforecast.",
